ChangeLog for the vkernel (vectorised kernel)
==============================================

Changes since [vkernel] 5d2bd0835 (compilation optimisation)

Storage / database / mp
-----------------------
storage::make reworked (single pack pass, no duplicate or empty columns,
linear concat_all and tuple_unique), a registry-backed world beside it for
runtime column lookup, compile-time and runtime database names
(NONOS_COMPILE_TIME_DATABASE), _nonos bindings split over NONOS_BIND_PARTS.

Narrowphase / collision
-----------------------
cxd vendored for the batch engine. Polytope relations (polytopexpolytope_r,
polytopefdisk_r, polytopedisk_r, mesh edges, manifolds by face clipping, EPA
depth), shape::polytope item, per-kind shape sets, polydisperse grains,
space-filter culling, cuNSearch sorted lists.

Simul / time stepping
---------------------
Systems and interactions as switchable sets, relation sets via
topology::bind. Moreau-Jean into kinds, theta split, GOSI at run time,
mark-based active set, storage::kernels and storage::schedule (the time step
with timings and dataflow). Action-based kernel and stage names.

Anitescu-Tasora / DEM / explicit
--------------------------------
AT: projected Gauss-Seidel CCP, warm start, APGD, Python bindings. DEM:
penalty springs with symplectic Euler, Python ExplicitDEMOSI. Both used with
MJ in the nscd cases, comparisons and shear studies; timed.py takes the
scheme and its parameters as run options.

Bindings / VTKHDF
-----------------
_nonos on the registry world by default, vnative backend for contact forces,
convex polygons and 2d_flow, glyph view, VTKHDF export of bodies, shapes,
statics, contacts and FEM.

Guix / CMake / tests / docs
---------------------------
Guix packaging fixes; CMake NONOS_COMPILE_TIME_DATABASE, config_samples and
cuda builds, ftime-trace commented out; cppunit and reference suites,
registry-world tests, NaN checks, FEM and polytope comparisons; docs on
manifolds, integrators and stability. Cleanup: sanitised mp.hpp and
pattern.hpp, warning and clang-format passes.
